  "title": "Erdős Problem #126",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(n)$ be maximal such that if $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{N}$ has $\\lvert A\\rvert=n$ then $\\prod_{a\neq b\\in A}(a+b)$ has at least $f(n)$ distinct prime factors. Is it true that $f(n)/\\log n\\to\\infty$?",
